<title>CANADA: McCain to buy Heinz unit for US$500 mln.</title>
<headline>McCain to buy Heinz unit for US$500 mln.</headline>
<dateline>FLORENCEVILLE, New Brunswick 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Privately held McCain Foods Ltd said on Friday that it agreed to buy the Ore-Ida food service from Ore-Ida Foods, Inc., a unit of H.J. Heinz Co, for US$500 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition, the largest in the history of (McCain's), represents C$728 million in annual sales and vaults McCain Foods into the number two position in the production of frozen French fries and potato specialties in the United States,&quot; it said in a news release.</p>
<p>McCain Foods is owned by one of the wealthiest families in Canada.</p>
</text>
